{
  "texts": [
    "About",
    "Work",
    "Wenjia SHI",
    "Integrated Designer",
    "Cooperate with Yuqing Wu, Xiangrui Zhou",
    "2023.09 -- 2024.01",
    "QUIPU",
    "Delicate emotions have long been submerged by massive digital information.",
    "Inspired by the traditional recording method, we use the modern technology to enable us to explore the possibility of linking the recording method with the entity in the modern context.",
    "#DataPhysicalization",
    "#InteractiveDesign",
    "According to documentary records and archaeological findings, humans began to use rope from the Neolithic Age at the latest, after a long heritage, has continued to the last century, and throughout the world, China, Japan,  Polynesia and other places have been prevalent.",
    "color",
    "number",
    "life",
    "calculate",
    "attachment",
    "war",
    "govern",
    "Black: death or disaster",
    "Yellow: gold",
    "White: silver or peace",
    "Bind objects to modify and describe them",
    "Give orders and tactics",
    "Record life events",
    "The number of knots represents the number",
    "Contracts and documents",
    "Arithmetic is performed by tying knots",
    "As the ancients tied knots with their own hands, the recorded events flowed with the knots and survived. Contemporary people are accustomed to the digital form of events, and their delicate emotions have long been submerged by massive digital information.",
    "\u200d",
    "We are trying to get people to re-perceive the relationship between the record itself and the physical material in the way that the traditional rope-tying records are.The form simulates the pious recording process, allowing the information to adhere to the material.",
    "Physicalizations can offer potential perceptual, cognitive, and communicative value that neither paper nor computer displays may be able to offer.",
    "Recorded physically, but stored digitally, to reminding people of the way information exists.",
    "Different Materials",
    "Small Colorful Cords",
    "Laser Cutting",
    "Hemp Rope",
    "Wool Rope",
    "Typography and LED Lighting",
    "Utilize Materials and Tech to make the knotting process natural and pure.",
    "Quipu",
    "recordings",
    "safely",
    "The",
    "are",
    "secured",
    "in",
    "Read Instructions",
    "Take out the rope",
    "Tying and Speaking",
    "Quipu will remember it for you now.",
    "Wait for result",
    "Look for secrets",
    "now",
    "Your",
    "a",
    "is",
    "story",
    "long-lasting",
    "knot",
    "1",
    "/",
    "6"
  ],
